<https://example.org/slice/unit:sha256:2ae21c3e423df11c496575167f5f21b6cc4b9bfcd4820e00060c850e9fb56281> <https://example.org/slice/scalarStart> "555"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<https://example.org/slice/unit:sha256:2ae21c3e423df11c496575167f5f21b6cc4b9bfcd4820e00060c850e9fb56281> <https://example.org/slice/section> <https://example.org/slice/section:sha256:f8e05ea31bfa1fea1794fb0745c3f2d211bff98b1ac1eac06aa10ec654b9aee8> .
<https://example.org/slice/unit:sha256:2ae21c3e423df11c496575167f5f21b6cc4b9bfcd4820e00060c850e9fb56281> <https://example.org/slice/text> "3. Between the Anvil and the Comb the shelf drops away in three steps,\nand each step keeps its own crowd: the first holds the banded urchins\nthat the fishers call pinheads, the second the pale fans 🐚 that close\nat a shadow and open again a slow count later, and the third nothing at\nall that a diver has yet named, only a cold green water that the light\ngives up on well before the floor of it is reached by any lamp we own." .
<https://example.org/slice/unit:sha256:2ae21c3e423df11c496575167f5f21b6cc4b9bfcd4820e00060c850e9fb56281> <https://example.org/slice/verse> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
